@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- PVI comprehensive health care insurance rules, for individual customers
-- (Quy tắc bảo hiểm chăm sóc sức khỏe toàn diện, Tổng công ty Bảo hiểm PVI).
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every other module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../source/raw/pvi-health.txt, the pdftotext -layout rendering of the PDF
-- whose sha256 is 89ce0df4...3fb49860, retrieved 2026-10-06 from a MIRROR on an agent's
-- website (moigioibaohiem.vn), not from PVI. A `src:N` comment quotes line N of that file,
-- generated by tools/vnsrc.py; no Vietnamese in a `src:` line is typed by hand.
--
-- Conventions for every module of this row:
-- * Money is Vietnamese dong (VND), a bare NUMBER.
-- * A percentage or a rate is a NUMBER written with L4's postfix `%` (50% is 0.5).
-- * Dates are DATEs. A period of days is counted in calendar days unless a rule says
--   otherwise; the one period of working days (Part V clause 4) says so where it is used.
-- * Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to
--   the fact, or a document on the claim file records it (a certificate, a hospital paper,
--   a doctor's conclusion, an invoice). Whether the fact makes a benefit payable is a rule,
--   and belongs in the module for the Part that says so.

§ `Nouns for the PVI comprehensive health care rules`

§§ `The parties`

-- Part I opens: the Rules are an agreement between PVI and the insured person named on the
-- certificate. A lawful beneficiary claims for the insured person in Part IV item 2 and Part V.
-- src:46 | Quy tắc bảo hiểm này là thoả thuận giữa Tổng công ty Bảo hiểm PVI (sau đây
-- src:47 | gọi là “Bảo hiểm PVI”) và Người được bảo hiểm có tên trên Giấy chứng nhận bảo
-- src:48 | hiểm.
DECLARE `A party` IS ONE OF
    `the insured person`                         -- Người được bảo hiểm
    `a lawful beneficiary`                       -- Người thụ hưởng hợp pháp
    `PVI`                                        -- Bảo hiểm PVI

-- What a party does under the Rules: the acts the regulative rules in
-- pvi-health-part1-general.l4 and pvi-health-part5-claims.l4 watch for.
DECLARE `An act under the Rules` IS ONE OF
    `submit the claim dossier`
    `pay the insurance money`
    `give written notice of early termination`
    `refuse to renew`
    `have the insured person medically examined`
    `refuse part or all of the claim`

§§ `The benefits`

-- Part III: two main benefits (A) and four supplementary benefits (B).
DECLARE `A benefit` IS ONE OF
    `personal accident`                          -- A.1 Bảo hiểm Tai nạn cá nhân
    `inpatient treatment`                        -- A.2 Điều trị nội trú do ốm đau, bệnh tật, tai nạn
    `outpatient treatment`                       -- B.1 Quyền lợi bổ sung 1
    `dental care`                                -- B.2 Quyền lợi bổ sung 2
    `maternity`                                  -- B.3 Quyền lợi bổ sung 3
    `death from illness`                         -- B.4 Quyền lợi bổ sung 4

-- Part I clause 1: where a benefit runs.
-- src:50 | 1. Phạm vi địa lý được bảo hiểm
-- src:52 | Đối với quyền lợi Bảo hiểm Tai nạn: Toàn thế giới.
-- src:54 | Đối với các quyền lợi khác: Việt Nam.
DECLARE `A geographic scope` IS ONE OF
    `the whole world`                            -- Toàn thế giới
    `Vietnam`                                    -- Việt Nam

-- What the event was. "ốm đau, bệnh tật" (sickness, illness) is one cause throughout the
-- Rules; pregnancy and childbirth are the cause of a maternity claim.
DECLARE `A cause` IS ONE OF
    `an accident`
    `an illness`
    `pregnancy or childbirth`

§§ `The insured person`

-- Part I clause 2.1: citizenship or residence.
-- src:60 | Người được bảo hiểm là công dân Việt Nam hoặc người nước ngoài cư trú tại Việt
-- src:61 | Nam,từ 15 (mười lăm) ngày tuổi đến 60 (sáu mươi) tuổi (tính theo lần sinh nhật gần
DECLARE `A residence status` IS ONE OF
    `a Vietnamese citizen`
    `a foreigner residing in Vietnam`
    `neither a Vietnamese citizen nor a foreigner residing in Vietnam`

-- Part I clause 2.2: the conditions under which PVI does not accept a person. Recorded as at
-- an instant, because the rule that reads them says WHEN (pvi-health-part1-general.l4, fork F5).
-- `rate of disability or permanent injury` is a fraction (50% is 0.5).
-- src:73 | 2.2. Bảo hiểm PVI không nhận bảo hiểm đối với các trường hợp sau:
-- src:75 | a. Người đang bị bệnh tâm thần, bệnh phong, ung thư.
-- src:77 | b. Người bị tàn tật hoặc thương tật vĩnh viễn từ 50% trở lên.
-- src:79 | c. Người đang trong thời gian điều trị bệnh hoặc thương tật.
DECLARE `A health status` HAS
    `suffering from a mental illness`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `suffering from leprosy`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `suffering from cancer`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `rate of disability or permanent injury`     IS A NUMBER
    `under treatment for an illness or injury`   IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `An insured person` HAS
    `date of birth`                              IS A DATE
    `a woman`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `residence status`                           IS A `A residence status`
    `health status when the insurance was taken out` IS A `A health status`
    -- Part I 2.1: insured with PVI without a break from the year the person was 60.
    `continuously insured with PVI since age 60` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The certificate`

-- One certificate (Hợp đồng / Giấy chứng nhận bảo hiểm) for one insurance year. The main
-- benefits A.1 and A.2 are on every certificate; the four supplementary benefits are taken
-- one by one. `benefits no higher than the previous certificate` is the comparison the
-- definition of continuous renewal turns on, as the two certificates themselves show it:
-- src:487 | - Tái tục liên tục: Là việc Hợp đồng / Giấy chứng nhận bảo hiểm mới có quyền lợi
-- src:488 | thấp hơn hoặc bằng quyền lợi bảo hiểm của Hợp đồng/ Giấy chứng nhận bảo
-- src:489 | hiểm mà Người được bảo hiểm đã tham gia trước đó và có ngày bắt đầu hiệu
-- src:490 | lực bảo hiểm vào đúng ngày kế tiếp sau ngày hết hạn bảo hiểm của Hợp đồng
-- src:491 | / Giấy chứng nhận bảo hiểm mà Người được bảo hiểm đã tham gia trước đó tại
-- src:492 | Bảo hiểm PVI.
DECLARE `A certificate period` HAS
    `start date`                                 IS A DATE
    `end date`                                   IS A DATE
    `includes outpatient treatment`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `includes dental care`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `includes maternity`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `includes death from illness`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `benefits no higher than the previous certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `premium paid in full and on time`           IS A BOOLEAN

-- The amounts the Rules leave to the schedule of benefits ("Bảng quyền lợi bảo hiểm Chăm sóc
-- Sức khỏe Toàn diện"), which is NOT part of the document. Every one is an input with no
-- default. `the sum insured` is the defined term Số tiền bảo hiểm, a maximum per insurance year
-- per insured person; each `limit ...` is a sub-limit (Giới hạn phụ) as the schedule states it
-- for the claim in hand (whether the schedule states it per event or per year is the
-- schedule's business: fork F14).
-- src:460 | - Số tiền bảo hiểm: Là số tiền bồi thường tối đa ghi trong Bảng quyền lợi bảo hiểm
-- src:461 | Chăm sóc Sức khỏe Toàn diện của Bảo hiểm PVI có thể được chi trả trong 01 năm
-- src:462 | bảo hiểm cho mỗi Người được bảo hiểm / Người thụ hưởng hợp pháp khi xảy ra
-- src:463 | sự kiện bảo hiểm.
-- src:465 | - Giới hạn trách nhiệm chi tiết (Giới hạn phụ): Là giới hạn bồi thường tối đa có thể
-- src:466 | trả cho từng quyền lợi bảo hiểm được quy định chi tiết trong Bảng quyền lợi bảo
-- src:467 | hiểm Chăm sóc Sức khỏe Toàn diện. Tuy nhiên tổng các giới hạn chi tiết không
-- src:468 | vượt quá Số tiền bảo hiểm.
DECLARE `The schedule of benefits` HAS
    `the sum insured`                            IS A NUMBER
    `sum insured for personal accident`          IS A NUMBER
    `limit for hospitalisation`                  IS A NUMBER
    `limit for surgery`                          IS A NUMBER
    `limit for outpatient treatment`             IS A NUMBER
    `sum insured for dental care`                IS A NUMBER
    `limit for maternity`                        IS A NUMBER
    `sum insured for death from illness`         IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `A certificate` HAS
    `this period`                                IS A `A certificate period`
    -- the insured person's earlier certificates at PVI, the most recent first
    `earlier periods at PVI`                     IS A LIST OF `A certificate period`
    -- "chương trình": the programmes are defined in the schedule, not in the document
    `programme`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `schedule`                                   IS A `The schedule of benefits`
    `premium`                                    IS A NUMBER
    -- the definition of the waiting period requires it to be shown on the certificate
    `shows the waiting periods of its benefits`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Part I 2.1, for an insured person under 18
    `on the same contract as the father or mother` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sums insured of the father or mother on that contract` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    -- Part I 5.2 and 10: the date an early termination took effect, if there was one
    `date of early termination`                  IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `The medical facility`

-- The kinds of facility the Rules distinguish: public hospitals (with or without an
-- international department) for the co-payment; "bệnh viện/ trung tâm y tế nhà nước, bệnh
-- viện tư nhân và quốc tế" for dental care in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City; clinics.
DECLARE `A kind of medical facility` IS ONE OF
    `a public hospital`                          -- Bệnh viện công lập
    `a private or international hospital`
    `a state medical centre`
    `a clinic`                                   -- Phòng khám
    `another medical facility`

-- The facts the definitions of a hospital (src:312-323) and a clinic (src:334-339), the
-- co-payment rule, the dental geography (src:690-698) and Part IV item 33 turn on.
DECLARE `A medical facility` HAS
    `kind`                                       IS A `A kind of medical facility`
    `the treatment was in its international department` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in Vietnam`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `in Hanoi or Ho Chi Minh City`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `licensed to operate lawfully`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `able to diagnose, treat and operate`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `equipped for inpatient treatment with daily monitoring` IS A BOOLEAN
    `solely for convalescence, the elderly, addiction, mental disorders or leprosy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid business licence and its own seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `able to examine, diagnose and treat`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `issues documents and invoices as the Ministry of Finance requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a cooperation agreement with PVI`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `on PVI's list of facilities refused for claims` IS A BOOLEAN
    `daily price of its cheapest single room`    IS A NUMBER

§§ `The treatment`

DECLARE `A room` IS ONE OF
    `a standard room`
    `an intensive care unit`                     -- phòng chăm sóc đặc biệt (ICU)
    `a room on request, a VIP room or a whole room booked` -- phòng theo yêu cầu, phòng VIP và bao phòng

-- One day of a hospital stay, with its costs split the way src:386-388 splits them.
DECLARE `A day in hospital` HAS
    `bed charge`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `other medical costs`                        IS A NUMBER
    `non-medical costs`                          IS A NUMBER

-- The facts the definitions in Part II (src:349-372) and the benefits in Part III read
-- about how the insured person was treated.
DECLARE `The treatment` HAS
    `admitted with the facility's admission procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an admission or discharge paper issued by a hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `stayed overnight in a hospital bed`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `continuous hours at the facility`           IS A NUMBER
    `bed charges incurred`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `for a diagnosed disease under a treatment protocol` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a surgery`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the surgery is on the Ministry of Health's list` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the surgeon holds a lawful practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dental treatment`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `indicated by the treating doctor`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the doctor is the insured person, or a spouse, parent, child or sibling of the insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a doctor's conclusion of a disease`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a specific treatment protocol`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the treating doctor concluded the disease is chronic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the room`                                   IS A `A room`
    `the days in hospital`                       IS A LIST OF `A day in hospital`
    `date of the last discharge from hospital`   IS A MAYBE DATE
    `days of the hospital stay before home care` IS A NUMBER

-- The facts the definition of a pre-existing disease (src:266-274) reads about the disease
-- the claim is for, before cover began.
DECLARE `The history of the disease` HAS
    `the disease existed before cover began`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of the last treatment before cover began` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `medical symptoms existed and originated before cover began` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The costs`

-- `paid under another insurance contract`: what another insurer has already paid for the
-- same costs (Part I clause 3). `already paid in this insurance year`: what PVI has paid the
-- insured person so far in the insurance year, against the sum insured.
DECLARE `The costs claimed` HAS
    `costs of the surgery`                       IS A NUMBER
    `other medical costs`                        IS A NUMBER
    `paid under another insurance contract`      IS A NUMBER
    `cost of the vitamins or minerals`           IS A NUMBER
    `cost of the treatment drugs`                IS A NUMBER
    `days of hospitalisation already paid in this insurance year` IS A NUMBER
    `already paid in this insurance year`        IS A NUMBER
    `scalings already paid in this insurance year` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Dental care`

-- Supplementary benefit 2, its list of services (src:670-688) and its exclusions (src:708-710).
DECLARE `A dental service` IS ONE OF
    `examination, X-ray and diagnosis`
    `scaling`
    `a filling with an ordinary material`        -- amalgam, composite or an equivalent
    `a filling with another material`
    `extraction of a diseased tooth or root`
    `root canal treatment`
    `treatment of gingivitis or periodontitis`
    `emergency treatment after an accident` HAS `hours after the accident` IS A NUMBER
    `making dentures`
    `cosmetic dental treatment or orthodontics`
    `another dental service`

DECLARE `A dental item` HAS
    `service`                                    IS A `A dental service`
    `cost`                                       IS A NUMBER

§§ `Maternity`

-- Supplementary benefit 3(a): the complications it names "bao gồm và không giới hạn" (including
-- and not limited to), so the list is open (src:730-748).
DECLARE `A complication of pregnancy` IS ONE OF
    `miscarriage or death of the foetus in the womb`
    `molar pregnancy`
    `ectopic pregnancy`
    `postpartum haemorrhage`
    `placenta retained in the womb after birth`
    `a therapeutic abortion`
    `a complication of one of these`
    `another complication of pregnancy or childbirth`

DECLARE `A maternity event` IS ONE OF
    `a complication` HAS `which` IS A `A complication of pregnancy`
    `a caesarean section` HAS `indicated by a doctor as necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a normal delivery`

§§ `Death or permanent injury`

-- Main benefit A.1 (death or permanent injury from an accident) and supplementary benefit B.4
-- (death from illness). The rate for a permanent injury is the rate a provincial-or-higher medical
-- assessment council concludes (definition of total permanent injury, src:239-242); the rate
-- for partial permanent injury comes from the annex "Bảng tỷ lệ trả tiền bảo hiểm thương tật",
-- which is NOT in the document as published: NOTHING means the injury is not listed in it.
DECLARE `The outcome of the accident` IS ONE OF
    `death of the insured person` HAS `date of death` IS A DATE
    `a permanent injury` HAS
        `date the injury was determined`         IS A DATE
        `rate concluded by a provincial or higher medical assessment council` IS A NUMBER
        `rate the annex gives for the injury`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `no death and no permanent injury`

DECLARE `The facts of death or permanent injury` HAS
    `outcome`                                    IS A `The outcome of the accident`
    `treatment of the injury has ended`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `already paid under Benefit 2 for the same accident` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Conditions the Rules name`

-- Every disease or condition the Rules name, with the line that names it. A diagnosis the Rules
-- do not name is `a condition the Rules do not name`. A claim lists the conditions the medical
-- documents record for the event (more than one may apply).
DECLARE `A condition` IS ONE OF
    -- Bệnh đặc biệt, the special diseases (src:287-293)
    `a benign tumour`
    `hypertension`
    `cardiovascular disease`
    `gastric ulcer`
    `polyarthritis`
    `intestinal ulcer`
    `hepatitis`
    `cirrhosis of the liver`
    `liver failure`
    `endometritis`
    `haemorrhoids`
    `stones in the urinary or biliary tract`
    `sinusitis`
    `diabetes`
    `Parkinson's disease`
    `a disease of the blood-forming system`
    `pulmonary insufficiency`
    `pneumothorax`
    `cerebrovascular disease`
    `stroke`
    `coma`
    `epilepsy`
    `Alzheimer's disease`
    `dementia`
    `a disorder of the thyroid or of pancreatic endocrine function`
    `a disorder of the adrenal glands`
    `an endocrine disorder`
    `lupus erythematosus`
    -- deemed pre-existing (src:276-285)
    `tonsillitis requiring tonsillectomy`
    `adenoiditis requiring curettage`
    `deviated nasal septum requiring surgery`
    `vestibular disorder`
    `degeneration of a joint, a vertebra or the spine`
    `otitis media requiring surgery`
    `herniated disc`
    `asthma`
    -- the 180-day waiting period for children (src:570-571)
    `bronchitis`
    `bronchiolitis`
    `pneumonia`
    -- Part IV items 13 to 28
    `a sexually transmitted disease`
    `AIDS`
    `HIV infection or a condition related to HIV`
    `malaria`
    `leprosy`
    `tuberculosis`
    `an occupational disease`
    `cancer or a malignant tumour`
    `bone marrow failure`
    `leukaemia`
    `kidney failure`
    `a congenital disease or defect`
    `a genetic disease`
    `a disease of genetic malformation`
    `congenital heart disease`
    `Down syndrome`
    `cleft lip`
    `cleft palate`
    `hydrocephalus`
    `anal stenosis`
    `phimosis`
    `congenital deviated septum`
    `a mental illness or a mental or behavioural disorder`
    `developmental delay`
    `attention deficit disorder`
    `autism`
    `snoring or sleep apnoea`
    `a sleep disorder`
    `insomnia`
    `physical asthenia`
    `neurasthenia`
    `exhaustion from overwork`
    `stress syndrome`
    `myopia`
    `hyperopia`
    `astigmatism`
    `natural deterioration of sight or hearing`
    `cataract`
    `rickets`
    `malnutrition`
    `obesity`
    `acne`
    `hair loss`
    `skin hyperpigmentation`
    `infertility`
    `impotence`
    `sexual dysfunction`
    `a torn meniscus`
    `a condition the Rules do not name`

§§ `Circumstances the Rules name`

-- Every other fact the exclusions of Part IV and of the supplementary benefits turn on, one
-- per limb, so a proviso is its own fact ("trừ khi ..." is never folded into the limb it
-- qualifies). A claim lists the circumstances its documents establish.
DECLARE `A circumstance` IS ONE OF
    -- item 2
    `caused by an intentional act of the insured person`
    `caused by an intentional act of the claiming beneficiary`
    `caused by an intentional act of another beneficiary`
    -- item 3
    `use of beer, alcohol, drugs or a similar stimulant`
    `a doctor or a competent authority concluded that use was the direct cause`
    -- item 4
    `treatment or care for drug or alcohol addiction`
    `use of medicine not as indicated by a doctor`
    -- item 5
    `treatment or surgery at the insured person's own request`
    `the treatment or surgery is normal treatment as the Ministry of Health regulates it`
    -- item 6
    `caused by war, civil war, a strike or terrorism`
    -- item 7
    `arising from chemical pollution, radioactive material or nuclear material`
    `arising from an epidemic`
    `arising from a natural disaster`
    -- item 8
    `the insured person intended suicide`
    `the insured person deliberately went into unnecessary danger`
    `to save a person or property`
    -- item 9
    `the insured person violated the law`
    `the insured person violated labour safety rules at the workplace`
    `a record of a competent authority confirms the violation`
    -- item 10
    `an injury from fighting`
    `proven to be lawful self-defence`
    -- item 11
    `taking part in aviation`
    `as a passenger`
    `taking part in military training exercises`
    `taking part in combat with the armed forces`
    -- item 12
    `training for or competing in a professional sport`
    `taking part in a race`
    -- item 16
    `dialysis or artificial kidney treatment`
    -- item 17
    `a surgery that existed before the start of the insurance term`
    -- item 20
    `a periodic or routine health check-up`
    `preventive treatment or preventive medication`
    `a periodic test or check after treatment`
    `the result of that test or check was normal`
    `a routine antenatal check-up`
    `care of a newborn baby`
    `vaccination`
    `a routine eye or hearing test`
    -- item 21
    `cosmetic treatment or plastic surgery`
    `reconstruction to restore the function of an organ injured by an accident in the insurance term`
    -- item 22
    `weight control treatment`
    -- item 23
    `rehabilitation treatment`
    `buying, maintaining or adjusting a prosthesis`
    `an implanted medical device`
    `a medical device used outside the body`
    -- item 24
    `family planning`
    `artificial insemination`
    `hormone replacement therapy`
    `a sex change`
    -- item 26
    `pre-natal or post-natal care`
    -- item 27
    `vitamins, minerals, functional foods, supplements, cosmeceuticals, cosmetics or medical preparations`
    `vitamins or minerals indicated by a doctor to treat a deficiency`
    `vitamins or minerals indicated by a doctor to support treatment`
    -- item 28
    `ligament reconstruction`
    -- item 29
    `examination or treatment at home`
    `home nursing by a licensed nurse immediately after discharge, as the treating doctor ordered`
    `treatment at a rehabilitation centre, sauna, spa, resort, convalescent home, hydrotherapy facility or similar`
    `natural methods of treatment`
    `a stay at an infirmary`
    -- item 30
    `an injury that existed before the start of the insurance`
    `an indication for surgery that existed before the start of the insurance`
    -- item 33
    `a prescription or test ordered by a doctor of a clinic that does not meet the definition`
    -- item 35
    `experimental treatment`
    `treatment not recognised by science`
    `a free treatment service`

§§ `The claim`

-- One claim: one event, one benefit claimed. `the date the event arose` is the date of the
-- accident, or the onset of the illness, or the event of the pregnancy (fork F11);
-- `the date of treatment` is the first day on which a cost was incurred (the date of
-- admission for a hospital stay, whose days follow it one by one).
DECLARE `A claim` HAS
    `the insured`                                IS AN `An insured person`
    `the certificate`                            IS A `A certificate`
    `the benefit claimed`                        IS A `A benefit`
    `the claimant`                               IS A `A party`
    `the cause`                                  IS A `A cause`
    `the date the event arose`                   IS A DATE
    `the date of treatment`                      IS A DATE
    `the facility`                               IS A `A medical facility`
    `the treatment`                              IS A `The treatment`
    `the conditions`                             IS A LIST OF `A condition`
    `the circumstances`                          IS A LIST OF `A circumstance`
    `the history of the disease`                 IS A `The history of the disease`
    `the costs`                                  IS A `The costs claimed`
    `the dental items`                           IS A LIST OF `A dental item`
    `the maternity event`                        IS A MAYBE `A maternity event`
    `the death or injury facts`                  IS A `The facts of death or permanent injury`
    -- Part V clause 1
    `an accident while driving a vehicle`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `someone else is authorised to receive the money` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Early termination`

-- Part I clause 5.2.
DECLARE `A notice of early termination` HAS
    `given by`                                   IS A `A party`
    `in writing`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `date given`                                 IS A DATE
    `date of termination`                        IS A DATE
    `because the insured person breached the duty to pay the premium` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a claim has been paid in the certificate's term` IS A BOOLEAN
    `premium paid in full`                       IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Claim documents`

-- Part V clause 1, one member per document the clause names.
DECLARE `A claim document` IS ONE OF
    `the request for payment`
    `the accident report certified by the agency, the local authority or the police`
    `the driving licence and the vehicle registration`
    `the discharge paper and the treatment sheet`
    `the surgery record`
    `the medical book, prescriptions and test results`
    `the original payment documents`
    `the death certificate and the confirmation of lawful inheritance`
    `a lawful power of attorney`

§§ `What the rules decide`

-- Why a claim fails: one member per ground the Rules give, the Part IV item numbers carried
-- as a payload so an answer cites its clause.
DECLARE `A ground of refusal` IS ONE OF
    `the premium was not paid in full and on time`
    `the benefit is not on the certificate`
    `the event did not arise in the insurance term`
    `the cost arose after PVI's liability ended`
    `the event arose in the waiting period`
    `the insured person was not eligible for the benefit`
    `outside the scope of the benefit` HAS `which requirement` IS A STRING
    `excluded by Part IV item` HAS `item` IS A NUMBER
    `excluded by the benefit's own exclusions` HAS `which` IS A STRING

-- Invalid input is rejected, not answered (EITHER, left side): the caller can fix it.
DECLARE `A problem with the facts` IS ONE OF
    `the sum of the sub-limits exceeds the sum insured`
    `the certificate's term is not one year`
    `an amount claimed is negative`
